'''Sástago''' ({{Literal translation|swamp}}; {{Langx|mxi|سَاسْتَاغُو|Sástagu}}) is a [[Boroughs of Castejón|borough]] of the [[Castejón Metropolis]], within the [[Concordia|Concordia conurbation]]. It is noted as being the location of some of the largest {{W|social housing|social}} and {{W|cooperative housing}} {{W|housing estate|estates}} in the [[Baliscan Confederation]].

The population of Sástago reached a historic high of 2.7 million in 1973 but then declined; between 1973 and 1999 it declined every year, falling to less than two million in 1999. The borough's population loss reflected the experience of most other core urban areas in the developed world that have not expanded their boundaries. Factors in the migration included {{W|deindustrialisation}}, [[Special Period|economic stagnation]], a widening transit and {{W|food desert}}, and widespread damage as a result of {{W|Soil liquefaction|liquefaction}} of the soil during the [[1982 Tava Morotí earthquake]].

After significant reconstruction, it's population began to climb again, reaching 2.5 million in 2019, before falling slightly in 2021 as a result of {{W|gentrification}}, the {{W|COVID-19 pandemic}}, and {{W|class warfare|community violence}} during the [[2021 Baliscan civil unrest]]. Since then, an influx of younger residents and immigrants has contributed to the growth of the borough, and the local communes have embarked on a massive {{W|urban renewal}} program to drastically improve {{W|quality of life}} in the borough, and it ultimately surpassed it's former peak population in 2025.
